description:
What is awkward: addressbook.rs:271-275 emits the addressBookHasContents SetError via SetErrorType::Custom('addressBookHasContents'.to_owned()). This is a string literal scattered in handler code. The same is true for the doc comment, the test assertion, and the README. A typo in any one place (Contents vs Content, etc.) becomes a silent wire-format mismatch with no compile-time signal.

The canonical sibling jmap-mail-server defines spec-mandated SetError types as typed enum variants in SetErrorType (e.g. 'mailboxHasChild', 'mailboxHasEmail', 'overQuota'). Per workspace cookie-cutter intent, addressBookHasContents should be a typed variant of SetErrorType, not a Custom string.

Suggested rewrite: in jmap-server (or jmap-contacts-types if SetErrorType is per-extension), add:
    pub enum SetErrorType {
        // ...
        AddressBookHasContents,
    }
…and use SetErrorType::AddressBookHasContents at the call site. This is a small change that prevents a class of typo-bug, makes the error type discoverable via IDE completion, and aligns with how the canonical sibling handles its spec-mandated SetError types.

Note: this is the only spec-mandated SetError type unique to contacts (RFC 9610 §7.4.1). It's worth doing right.
